    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "24f36332_5a76261f",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 930,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-16T15:28:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Probably not.  \n\nI\u0027m waffling about removing the ready transition though since it causes issues with the moshi.  We report discard one cycle before the new message is received in the PE, so we can go from ready to already trying to start a different AMS in this case, which seems undesirable.  If we set a discard flag, it would slow down the PE process to match the PRL\u0027s pace here more.  Thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "1e2980a5_cbfcc8ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 930,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 930,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "2f32dd48ad71741414904abf295ba7645006b393",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eaed7c6c_38033ce6",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 930,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-17T20:34:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like we should add logic to have a cooldown period after a discard message has occured. That would make less depending on how often or behind/ahead the PRL is from the PE",
      "parentUuid": "24f36332_5a76261f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 930,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 930,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "2f32dd48ad71741414904abf295ba7645006b393",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41215423_32ac915a",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 930,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-17T21:51:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this is where I\u0027m seeing the wisdom of the spec just transitioning on message receive, because that ensures the PE knows that the message was discarded AND there\u0027s something new to process at the same time.\n\nFunctionally speaking, the only thing I need the PE to do on discard is clear this flag so we don\u0027t set NG again in the PRL_Tx.  That change by itself should fix our issue of presenting NG and confusing the port partners.  The rest is hopefully supposed to be helpful changes to unify how we\u0027re dealing with things.",
      "parentUuid": "eaed7c6c_38033ce6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 930,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 930,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "2f32dd48ad71741414904abf295ba7645006b393",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f86368a_958d6ffb",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 930,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-24T16:06:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, removing set_state here.  Verified we don\u0027t seem to hit issues with timing on the transitions, though if we wanted to be defensive we could have ready wait for msg received on discard, then clear discard.",
      "parentUuid": "41215423_32ac915a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 930,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 930,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "2f32dd48ad71741414904abf295ba7645006b393",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
