    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a3ec859a_deaef6b7",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-16T15:28:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could probably use this one, b/157228506.  I can update the comment for it. \n\nThere\u0027s a chart for what to do on unexpected message reception during an AMS, which I believe is essentially what we\u0027d have going on if we discarded mid-AMS.  It\u0027ll be a soft reset, hard reset, or going back to ready depending on whether the AMS is interruptible or involves power transitioning. We could either try addressing this via flags telling this function what to do, or having the discard flag report to the PE states and let them react accordingly.",
      "parentUuid": "9a600b2c_4424067a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 938,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "2f32dd48ad71741414904abf295ba7645006b393",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "427d610d_231c0328",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 938,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-17T20:34:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could go either way, but I slightly lean towards letting each state handle its own error path  (but that would cost more code size)\n\nIf there are only 3 differnet outcomes, maybe it is worth each child state setting which error hanlding they need and then common code can do it. I think we just have to play around with what looks best",
      "parentUuid": "a3ec859a_deaef6b7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 938,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 938,
        "endChar": 16
